    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FK94NRG8x7zRDHP6w2r8ca)_\n\nThe small form of #254 (removed in #259) that Sia chose after finding the startup hang came from the vterm/fish setup, not `svg-tag-mode`.\n\n- `M-x sp-org-heading-svg-tags-mode` (in `sp-faces`, doc and tangled `.el`) draws the tags at the end of an Org heading as stock `svg-tag-mode` tags, in the current buffer only.\n- **Off by default, nothing hooked, nothing runs at start.** It reuses the `svg-tag-mode` already declared in `sp-faces`; no new package, no `load-path`, no theme hook.\n- No tag-group colours, palette or emoji. The tag face is `org-tag`.\n- `#+filetags:` lines and TODO keywords are untouched: a match only counts inside the tags group of a heading (group 5 of `org-complex-heading-regexp`).\n- Stays off with a message in a terminal frame or without SVG.\n\nChecked in headless Emacs 29.3 with the real `svg-tag-mode` and a stub for the image: on `#+filetags: :a:b:` / `* TODO Title: x :p:q_1:` / `body a:b:` only the heading tags get a display. **Not run in a graphic frame.**\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9xYXWjL6cySxZHmKU)_",
    "changed_files": 3,
